  "id": "Compound::DB00493 - Gene::6565",
  "verbalization": "Cefotaxime, a member of the cephalosporin class, is consistently linked to Slc15a2 through a shared biological pathway. The evidence suggests that Cefotaxime, as part of the broader cephalosporin family, binds to Slc15a2 via its interaction with the Cephalosporin Antibiotic category. This relationship is supported by multiple paths, all of which highlight the hierarchical inclusion of Cefotaxime within cephalosporins and the direct binding of these antibiotics to Slc15a2. The lowest common ancestors across all paths reinforce the central role of cephalosporins in mediating this interaction, suggesting a conserved mechanism. The integration of these pathways implies that the interaction between Cefotaxime and Slc15a2 is likely driven by a common structural or functional property of cephalosporins, which may involve their ability to modulate ion transport or cellular processes through the Slc15a2 transporter.",
